#N canvas 20 20 1700 1060 12;
#X text 20 20 volca-probe -- Phase 9 Step 0A2. Does the Volca FM answer at all \, and are its parameter CCs reachable? Load as a THIRD patch after mother.pd and main.pd \, per ref/conventions.md. It sends on Pd channel 49 -- device 4 \, the USB Uno interface \, the Volca's own channel 1., f 76;
#X text 20 110 IT DIAGNOSES THE SETTING RATHER THAN REQUIRING IT. MIDI RX ShortMessage gates every CC 40-50 and NOTHING ELSE \, so notes are the control: notes + CC working means the setting is already on \; notes working while CC does nothing IS that setting being off \; silence from both is cabling or channel and not a setting at all. Prove the channel \, then believe the silence -- items 196 and 198., f 76;
#X text 20 240 SELF-DRIVING ON PURPOSE. This is a first-contact probe rather than a bench -- there is nothing to step through \, and the only judgement is whether you HEAR it. Every stage prints before it fires., f 76;
#X obj 20 380 loadbang;
#X obj 20 420 del 2000;
#X obj 20 470 t b b b b;
#X msg 900 520 49;
#X obj 900 570 t f f;
#X msg 640 520 40;
#X obj 20 800 makenote 100 400;
#X obj 20 860 noteout;
#X obj 640 800 ctlout;
#X obj 1180 640 print VOLCA;
#X msg 400 530 PHASE-1 three notes 48 52 55 -- if you hear nothing the path is dead;
#X obj 20 530 t b b b;
#X obj 20 580 del 300;
#X msg 20 630 48;
#X obj 120 580 del 1300;
#X msg 120 630 52;
#X obj 220 580 del 2300;
#X msg 220 630 55;
#X obj 400 380 del 5000;
#X obj 400 430 t b b;
#X msg 400 620 PHASE-2 CC 40 transpose -- hold is not needed \, each step retriggers note 48;
#X obj 400 680 del 300;
#X msg 400 730 0;
#X obj 500 680 del 1300;
#X msg 500 730 127;
#X obj 600 680 del 2300;
#X msg 600 730 64;
#X obj 760 380 del 12000;
#X msg 760 430 PHASE-3 done -- if phase 1 played and phase 2 changed the pitch \, both work;
#X text 1180 700 THE CHANNEL AND THE CONTROLLER NUMBER GO IN COLD \, off the RIGHTMOST outlets \, so both are stored before any value arrives. Same pattern item 63 proved for midiout -- the port set into the cold inlet at load rather than as a creation argument \, because Pd 0.49 does not warn about extra creation args and a clean load would prove nothing either way., f 60;
#X text 1180 860 noteout inlets are pitch \, velocity \, channel. ctlout inlets are value \, controller \, channel. makenote handles the note-offs \, so nothing here can leave the Volca droning., f 60;
#X text 20 920 ⚠️ EVERY PRINT IS BEHIND THE 2000 ms del \, which is deploy.sh's rule -- but this file is never deployed \, so that is belt and braces rather than a requirement. It also covers loadbang firing before ALSA is wired., f 76;
